{"id":"mahabharata-4-027","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":27,"title":"सप्तविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 27 · Bhishma's counsel","summary":{"en":"Bhishma says that wherever Yudhishthira lives, the people will be generous, truthful and content, the rains will fall in season and the land will prosper. By such signs, he says, the Pandavas may be found, and Duryodhana should act on this quickly.","kn":"ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಎಲ್ಲಿ ವಾಸಿಸುತ್ತಾನೋ ಅಲ್ಲಿ ಜನರು ಉದಾರಿಗಳೂ ಸತ್ಯವಂತರೂ ತೃಪ್ತರೂ ಆಗಿರುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಕಾಲಕ್ಕೆ ಮಳೆ ಬಂದು ನಾಡು ಸಮೃದ್ಧವಾಗುತ್ತದೆ ಎಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಇಂಥ ಲಕ್ಷಣಗಳಿಂದ ಪಾಂಡವರನ್ನು ಕಂಡುಹಿಡಿಯಬಹುದು, ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನು ಬೇಗ ಕಾರ್ಯಪ್ರವೃತ್ತನಾಗಲಿ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीष्म कहते हैं कि जहाँ युधिष्ठिर रहते हैं वहाँ लोग उदार, सत्यवादी और सन्तुष्ट होंगे, समय पर वर्षा होगी और देश समृद्ध होगा। वे कहते हैं कि ऐसे लक्षणों से पाण्डवों को पाया जा सकता है, और दुर्योधन को शीघ्र इस पर कार्य करना चाहिए।","te":"యుధిష్ఠిరుడు ఎక్కడ నివసిస్తాడో అక్కడ ప్రజలు ఉదారులు, సత్యవంతులు, సంతృప్తులుగా ఉంటారని, సకాలంలో వర్షాలు కురిసి దేశం సమృద్ధమవుతుందని భీష్ముడు అంటాడు. ఇలాంటి లక్షణాలతో పాండవులను కనుగొనవచ్చని, దుర్యోధనుడు త్వరగా చర్య తీసుకోవాలని చెబుతాడు.","ta":"யுதிஷ்டிரர் எங்கு வாழ்கிறாரோ அங்கு மக்கள் தாராளமும் உண்மையும் மனநிறைவும் உள்ளவர்களாக இருப்பார்கள், பருவத்தில் மழை பெய்து நாடு செழிக்கும் என்று பீஷ்மர் சொல்கிறார். இத்தகைய அடையாளங்களால் பாண்டவர்களைக் கண்டுபிடிக்கலாம், துரியோதனன் விரைந்து செயல்பட வேண்டும் என்கிறார்.","ml":"യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ താമസിക്കുന്നിടത്തെല്ലാം ജനങ്ങൾ ഉദാരരും സത്യസന്ധരും സംതൃപ്തരുമായിരിക്കുമെന്നും, മഴ കാലത്തിന് പെയ്യുകയും ദേശം സമൃദ്ധമാകുകയും ചെയ്യുമെന്നും ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. ഈ ലക്ഷണങ്ങളിലൂടെ പാണ്ഡവരെ കണ്ടെത്താനാകുമെന്നും, ദുര്യോധനൻ വേഗം ഇതിൽ പ്രവർത്തിക്കണമെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.27; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"गोग्रहणपर्व","titleEn":"Gograhana Parva (The cattle raid)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः शांतनवो भीष्मो भरतानां पितामहः ।\nश्रुतवान्देशकालज्ञस्तत्त्वज्ञः सर्वधर्मवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhishma, son of Shantanu, grandfather of the Bharatas, learned, knowing place and time, knowing the truth and all dharma,"}},{"n":2,"text":"आचार्यवाक्योपरमे तद्वाक्यमभिसंदधत् ।\nहितार्थं स उवाचेमां भारतीं भारतान्प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"when the teacher had finished speaking, bearing his words in mind, spoke to the Bharatas for their good these words,"}},{"n":3,"text":"युधिष्ठिरे समासक्तां धर्मज्ञे धर्मसंश्रिताम् ।\nअसत्सु दुर्लभां नित्यं सतां चाभिमतां सदा ।\nभीष्मः समवदत्तत्र गिरं साधुभिरर्चिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"words attached to Yudhishthira, who knows dharma, resting on dharma, always hard for the wicked to find and always approved by the good; such words, praised by the virtuous, Bhishma spoke there."}},{"n":4,"text":"यथैष ब्राह्मणः प्राह द्रोणः सर्वार्थतत्त्ववित् ।\nसर्वलक्षणसंपन्ना नाशं नार्हन्ति पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said: As this brahmin Drona, who knows the truth of all matters, has said, the Pandavas, endowed with every good sign, do not deserve ruin."}},{"n":5,"text":"श्रुतवृत्तोपसंपन्नाः साधुव्रतसमन्विताः ।\nवृद्धानुशासने मग्नाः सत्यव्रतपरायणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are rich in learning and conduct, devoted to good vows, immersed in the teaching of their elders and devoted to truth."}},{"n":6,"text":"समयं समयज्ञास्ते पालयन्तः शुचिव्रताः ।\nनावसीदितुमर्हन्ति उद्वहन्तः सतां धुरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing the terms, they keep the agreement and keep their vows pure; bearing the burden of the good, they do not deserve to sink."}},{"n":7,"text":"धर्मतश्चैव गुप्तास्ते स्ववीर्येण च पाण्डवाः ।\nन नाशमधिगच्छेयुरिति मे धीयते मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Guarded by dharma and by their own valor, the Pandavas will not meet destruction; so my mind holds."}},{"n":8,"text":"तत्र बुद्धिं प्रणेष्यामि पाण्डवान्प्रति भारत ।\nन तु नीतिः सुनीतस्य शक्यतेऽन्वेषितुं परैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, I shall apply my thought to the Pandavas, but the policy of one well guided in policy cannot be traced out by others."}},{"n":9,"text":"यत्तु शक्यमिहास्माभिस्तान्वै संचिन्त्य पाण्डवान् ।\nबुद्ध्या प्रवक्तुं न द्रोहात्प्रवक्ष्यामि निबोध तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall tell you what we can say here, considering those Pandavas with understanding and not out of malice; listen."}},{"n":10,"text":"सा त्वियं साधु वक्तव्या न त्वनीतिः कथंचन ।\nवृद्धानुशासने तात तिष्ठतः सत्यशीलिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This must be said well and by no means unwisely, dear son, to one who keeps to the teaching of elders and is truthful."}},{"n":11,"text":"अवश्यं त्विह धीरेण सतां मध्ये विवक्षता ।\nयथामति विवक्तव्यं सर्वशो धर्मलिप्सया ॥","meaning":{"en":"A steady person speaking among the good should always say, as his understanding goes, whatever he says from a wish for dharma."}},{"n":12,"text":"तत्र नाहं तथा मन्ये यथायमितरो जनः ।\nपुरे जनपदे वापि यत्र राजा युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this matter I do not think as ordinary people do, about city or country where King Yudhishthira lives."}},{"n":13,"text":"नासूयको न चापीर्षुर्नातिवादी न मत्सरी ।\nभविष्यति जनस्तत्र स्वं स्वं धर्ममनुव्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that place the people will not be envious or jealous or boastful or spiteful, but each will follow his own dharma."}},{"n":14,"text":"ब्रह्मघोषाश्च भूयांसः पूर्णाहुत्यस्तथैव च ।\nक्रतवश्च भविष्यन्ति भूयांसो भूरिदक्षिणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There will be much Vedic recitation and full offerings, and many sacrifices with abundant fees."}},{"n":15,"text":"सदा च तत्र पर्जन्यः सम्यग्वर्षी न संशयः ।\nसंपन्नसस्या च मही निरीतीका भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the rain-cloud will always rain well, no doubt, and the earth will be rich in crops and free of calamity."}},{"n":16,"text":"रसवन्ति च धान्यानि गुणवन्ति फलानि च ।\nगन्धवन्ति च माल्यानि शुभशब्दा च भारती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grains will be tasty, fruits excellent, garlands fragrant, and speech full of auspicious sounds."}},{"n":17,"text":"वायुश्च सुखसंस्पर्शो निष्प्रतीपं च दर्शनम् ।\nभयं नाभ्याविशेत्तत्र यत्र राजा युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wind will be pleasant to the touch, the sight unobstructed, and fear will not enter where King Yudhishthira is."}},{"n":18,"text":"गावश्च बहुलास्तत्र न कृशा न च दुर्दुहाः ।\nपयांसि दधिसर्पींषि रसवन्ति हितानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cows will be plentiful there, neither thin nor hard to milk; milk, curds and ghee will be tasty and wholesome."}},{"n":19,"text":"गुणवन्ति च पानानि भोज्यानि रसवन्ति च ।\nतत्र देशे भविष्यन्ति यत्र राजा युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drinks will be good and foods tasty in the country where King Yudhishthira lives."}},{"n":20,"text":"रसाः स्पर्शाश्च गन्धाश्च शब्दाश्चापि गुणान्विताः ।\nदृश्यानि च प्रसन्नानि यत्र राजा युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tastes, touches, scents and sounds will be full of excellence, and sights pleasing, where Yudhishthira is king."}},{"n":21,"text":"स्वैः स्वैर्गुणैः सुसंयुक्तास्तस्मिन्वर्षे त्रयोदशे ।\nदेशे तस्मिन्भविष्यन्ति तात पाण्डवसंयुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that thirteenth year, dear son, they will each be rich in their own qualities in the land that holds the Pandavas."}},{"n":22,"text":"संप्रीतिमाञ्जनस्तत्र संतुष्टः शुचिरव्ययः ।\nदेवतातिथिपूजासु सर्वभूतानुरागवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The people there will be happy, content, pure and undiminished, reverent toward gods and guests, and loving toward all beings."}},{"n":23,"text":"इष्टदानो महोत्साहः शश्वद्धर्मपरायणः ।\nअशुभद्विट्शुभप्रेप्सुर्नित्ययज्ञः शुभव्रतः ।\nभविष्यति जनस्तत्र यत्र राजा युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Generous in sacrifice, full of energy, always devoted to dharma, hating evil and desiring good, constant in sacrifice and firm in good vows: such will be the people where King Yudhishthira is."}},{"n":24,"text":"त्यक्तवाक्यानृतस्तात शुभकल्याणमङ्गलः ।\nशुभार्थेप्सुः शुभमतिर्यत्र राजा युधिष्ठिरः ।\nभविष्यति जनस्तत्र नित्यं चेष्टप्रियव्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Giving up lies in speech, full of goodness and blessing, wishing for good ends, with good minds, constant in the vows they love: such will be the people where King Yudhishthira is."}},{"n":25,"text":"धर्मात्मा स तदादृश्यः सोऽपि तात द्विजातिभिः ।\nकिं पुनः प्राकृतैः पार्थः शक्यो विज्ञातुमन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That righteous man would thus be unseen even by the twice-born, dear son; how then could ordinary people finally recognize Partha?"}},{"n":26,"text":"यस्मिन्सत्यं धृतिर्दानं परा शान्तिर्ध्रुवा क्षमा ।\nह्रीः श्रीः कीर्तिः परं तेज आनृशंस्यमथार्जवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In him are truth, steadiness, generosity, perfect calm, constancy, patience, modesty, glory, fame, great radiance, mercy and honesty."}},{"n":27,"text":"तस्मात्तत्र निवासं तु छन्नं सत्रेण धीमतः ।\nगतिं वा परमां तस्य नोत्सहे वक्तुमन्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore I cannot say otherwise than that the wise man lives hidden in some such place, or what his highest course is."}},{"n":28,"text":"एवमेतत्तु संचिन्त्य यत्कृतं मन्यसे हितम् ।\nतत्क्षिप्रं कुरु कौरव्य यद्येवं श्रद्दधासि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having thought this over, do quickly, Kaurava, whatever you think is good, if you believe me."}}]}]}